 "history": "Men at almost every level wore the frock for work and informal wear: plain cloth, a turn-down collar and an easy cut, in drab, brown, grey, blue or green [R20][M3]. In the Mohawk valley the Palatine farmers and their militia wore the same coats as their English neighbours; no dress source specific to German Flatts survives, so this follows rural Pennsylvania German and general 1750s evidence (Goschenhoppen Historians; the V&A's 1750s suit for the cut).",
